2026-08-06\\n\\n## What remains out of scope\\n\\nThis validation does not redefine the quota policy or introduce a soft buffer above the hard halt. Those questions, if they arise later, are separate from this acceptance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 purpos confirm that t022 s disk usag monitor actual stop further write onc the configur quota is reach not mere that the loop is run sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 verif diana ran the monitor against a configur quota and check write behavior at the threshold the monitor halt further write a requir that initi behavior wa accept a meet the quota requir for this pas sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 outcom complet quota halt behavior is verifi for the configur threshold check here sourc id src gdoc 36 storag quota halt valid owner diana document key doc 2036 last updat 2026 08 06 what remain out of scope this valid doe not redefin the quota polici or introduc a soft buffer abov the hard halt those question if they aris later are separ from this accept\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eea7a8d68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"id\": \"b8f1c98ded3168bf\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3161409706832269, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10429107240460987, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8104574, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eea7a8d68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-06-Storage-Quota-Halt-Validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 834, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:45\", \"token_count\": 328, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-22\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Storage Quota Management Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:30] Evan**: Starting on storage quota management. We need to keep `cipherdoc` from filling up the disk on these workstations, especially on large batch jobs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:39] Evan**: Implementing a disk-usage monitor loop. It'll check available space before starting any new redaction job.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:41] Alice**: What's the threshold?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:08] Evan**: Going with a hard 500MB floor for now. If free space drops below that, the engine pauses and alerts the user.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:26] Diana**: We also need a way to clear the cache — the `/tmp` folder doesn't always clean up properly after a crash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:41] Evan**: I'll add a purge-cache option and run a sweep on startup too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:44] Evan**: @Bob, can we get a hook in the `FileStreamer` to report current disk usage for the active job?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:30] Bob**: Sure, I'll add a `get_quota_usage()` method to the stream controller.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 22 slack thread storag quota manag design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 09 30 evan start on storag quota manag we need to keep cipherdoc from fill up the disk on these workstat especi on larg batch job 2026 08 04 09 39 evan implement a disk usag monitor loop it ll check avail space befor start ani new redact job 2026 08 04 09 41 alic what s the threshold 2026 08 04 10 08 evan go with a hard 500mb floor for now if free space drop below that the engin paus and alert the user 2026 08 04 10 26 diana we also need a way to clear the cach the tmp folder doesn t alway clean up proper after a crash 2026 08 04 10 41 evan i ll add a purg cach option and run a sweep on startup too 2026 08 04 10 44 evan bob can we get a hook in the filestream to report current disk usag for the activ job 2026 08 04 11 30 bob sure i ll add a get _ quota _ usag method to the stream control\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edd22bd48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"id\": \"d46709d1a43ccf8a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29935535494915066, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0808460499273581, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8092104, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edd22bd48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-storage-quota-monitor.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1088, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:01\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Monitor loop\\n\\nOn 2026-08-04 Evan landed a live disk-usage monitor that watches free space during batch processing and is meant to stop further writes once a configured quota is crossed. The loop is in place; it is not yet a signed-off gate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-16\\n\\n# Storage Quota — Disk-Usage Monitor\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2016\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-05 (retrospective of 2026-08-04)\\n\\nLarge batch runs can exhaust local disk if nothing caps write volume. T022 opened to add a storage quota for that reason.\\n\\n## Still open\\n\\nNobody has yet confirmed that the monitor actually halts writes at the configured threshold. Until that check lands, T022 stays Active.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason monitor loop on 2026 08 04 evan land a live disk usag monitor that watch free space dure batch process and is meant to stop further write onc a configur quota is cross the loop is in place it is not yet a sign off gate sourc id src gdoc 16 storag quota disk usag monitor owner evan document key doc 2016 last updat 2026 08 05 retrospect of 2026 08 04 larg batch run can exhaust local disk if noth cap write volum t022 open to add a storag quota for that reason still open nobodi ha yet confirm that the monitor actual halt write at the configur threshold until that check land t022 stay activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eeb174248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"id\": \"9d33aa17d4e760e3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29162540026475675, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07387284323536683, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7997147, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eeb174248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-05-Storage-Quota-Management-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 688, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:37\", \"token_count\": 274, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"7d969f7c78a9200e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2743689739763555, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07045422710907931, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75017005, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:23\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-61\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch I/O Race\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-25\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:20] Diana**: Blocker on the async batch path. Under concurrent load the workers hit an I/O race and throughput drops — roughly 10% versus the sync baseline.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:21] Bob**: Is that the scheduler shell or the workers we just added?\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:23] Diana**: The workers. Scheduler alone was fine; once concurrent workers share I/O with the existing multi-thread batch pool, the race shows up.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 11:48] Charlie**: That pool is the multi-thread path. Mixing it with async workers without coordinating I/O was going to bite us.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:50] Alice**: Then we stop here. I have to leave the async batch work blocked until the race with the multi-thread pool is sorted. A 10% hit is not shippable.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:51] Bob**: Ok.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:52] Bob**: Fair. I'll hold further async work until we understand the interaction with that pool.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:54] Diana**: I'll capture the repro steps so we can re-run once there's a candidate fix.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 61 slack thread async batch i o race channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 25 2026 08 25 10 20 diana blocker on the async batch path under concurr load the worker hit an i o race and throughput drop rough 10 versus the sync baselin 2026 08 25 10 21 bob is that the schedul shell or the worker we just ad 2026 08 25 10 23 diana the worker schedul alon wa fine onc concurr worker share i o with the exist multi thread batch pool the race show up 2026 08 25 11 48 charli that pool is the multi thread path mix it with async worker without coordin i o wa go to bite u 2026 08 25 12 50 alic then we stop here i have to leav the async batch work block until the race with the multi thread pool is sort a 10 hit is not shippabl 2026 08 25 12 51 bob ok 2026 08 25 12 52 bob fair i ll hold further async work until we understand the interact with that pool 2026 08 25 12 54 diana i ll captur the repro step so we can re run onc there s a candid fix\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee1d78008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"id\": \"d35a1fb74d2e1aff\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2627188009763555, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07045422710907931, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71133614, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee1d78008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1123, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:49\", \"token_count\": 349, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"4951fb04269a3c9b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2619968569763555, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07045422710907931, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70892966, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:57\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-43\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:30] Bob**: Reopening large-file chunking. On long-running batches with files over 2GB, memory is still leaking even though the chunked-read path is supposedly done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:31] Charlie**: That's odd, chunking should mean each buffer gets dropped once we move past it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:41] Bob**: It's not the page buffers themselves — something else is holding a reference and keeping them from being freed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:08] Diana**: I can reproduce it in QA too. Memory climbs steadily and the process eventually gets killed on the larger inputs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:20] Charlie**: I'll dig into what's still holding those references. Reopening this until we find it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 43 slack thread larg file chunk reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 10 30 bob reopen larg file chunk on long run batch with file over 2gb memori is still leak even though the chunk read path is suppos done 2026 08 18 10 31 charli that s odd chunk should mean each buffer get drop onc we move past it 2026 08 18 10 41 bob it s not the page buffer themselv someth els is hold a refer and keep them from be freed 2026 08 18 11 08 diana i can reproduc it in qa too memori climb steadili and the process eventu get kill on the larger input 2026 08 18 11 20 charli i ll dig into what s still hold those refer reopen this until we find it\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0cc0a08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"fc180423f1c2406b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2612550269293623, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.039109152756231884, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7795954, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0cc0a08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:06\", \"token_count\": 252, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"SRC-SLACK-23 Storage Quota Halt CIPH-32 hard halt 500MB later evidence reopened\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"As of 2026-09-22, **CIPH-32/T022 is reopened and active**; its quota-monitor buffer refactor still needs verification. (`WS-07`, last updated 2026-09-22)\n\nIt was reopened on September 15 after **production-like batches hit the 500 MB hard halt before doing useful work**—the flat cutoff had no soft buffer. (`SRC-SLACK-23`)\n\nThe change underway is a **10% buffer tolerance above quota** instead of an immediate 500 MB hard halt. Operations is also setting the production free-disk baseline to **2 GB, not 500 MB**. (`SRC-SLACK-23`; `SRC-CU-CIPH-32`; `CMT-2026-09-003`)"}}
